{"diagnosis": "Loopback UART read returned reg_dat_do 0xff instead of expected 0xa5, causing tohost FAIL 0xdead with TRAP uart data mismatch. ser_tx idles from send_pattern[0], but reset loads send_pattern <= ~1 whose LSB is 0, driving a false start and latching 0xff in recv_buf_data. Root cause is the wrong reset constant on line 114; idle must be ~0 to hold ser_tx high.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -112,5 +112,5 @@
 		send_divcnt <= send_divcnt + 1;
 		if (!resetn) begin
-			send_pattern <= ~1;
+			send_pattern <= ~0;
 			send_bitcnt <= 0;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (was FAIL 0xdead) with loopback 0xa5 matched, TRAP uart data mismatch gone"}

